inevitably|unavoidably|ADVERB|Unavoidably|In a way that cannot be prevented or avoided.|không thể tránh khỏi; tất yếu|Extra work inevitably takes extra time.|Thêm công việc tất yếu cần thêm thời gian.|Sentence or manner adverb.|0
impulse|urge|NOUN|Sudden urge|A sudden desire to act, often without careful thought.|sự thôi thúc; cơn bốc đồng|She resisted the impulse to interrupt.|Cô ấy kiềm chế sự thôi thúc muốn ngắt lời.|Countable; impulse to do.|-
messenger|carrier|NOUN|Person delivering a message|Someone who carries or delivers information to another person.|người đưa tin; sứ giả|A messenger brought the invitation to the office.|Một người đưa tin mang thư mời tới văn phòng.|Countable person, not message itself.|-
if|condition|CONJUNCTION|Introduce a condition|Used to introduce a condition for another event.|nếu|If it rains, we will meet indoors.|Nếu trời mưa, chúng ta sẽ gặp trong nhà.|If clause present with future main clause.|0
if|whether|CONJUNCTION|Introduce an indirect question|Used to introduce uncertainty about whether something is true.|liệu; có hay không|She asked if the shop was open.|Cô ấy hỏi cửa hàng có mở cửa không.|Indirect question; no question inversion.|1
mourn|grieve|VERB|Feel sorrow after loss|To feel or show deep sadness after someone dies or something is lost.|thương tiếc; đau buồn|The village mourned its beloved teacher.|Ngôi làng thương tiếc người thầy kính yêu.|Mourn someone or mourn for.|-
